  "body": "The `createHTML` function in the [TrustedTypePolicy](https://w3c.github.io/trusted-types/dist/spec/#trusted-type-policy) takes a string input and is supposed to return a sanitized version of that HTML. This is a pretty obvious use case fo the Sanitizer API. However since we removed the methods for actually sanitizing to a string from the API, there is actually no direct way of doing this. One of the main reasons for the removal were concerns about reparsing HTML actually being unsafe. I think we might want to think about some way of integrating the Sanitizer and Trusted Types that wouldn't involve any reparsing and intermediate HTML strings.\n\n/cc @lukewarlow @fred-wang",
